what The Glow ident arc's next fall is the `rm.max_name_len` PAIR the scan's own ceiling comment names as the cheaper door, and I read it at the door rather than taking the line's word: `glow/lower_shape.rye` and `glow/lower_named_cast.rye` declare `fn zig_safe_ident` bodies that are byte-identical at md5 `4484b371`, carrying 14 and 15 call sites, and both already answer `u32` rather than the `usize` 23 of the original 29 answered -- so this pair costs no width repair and the whole lap is the delegation. Both files' `LowerError` sets carry `BadIdent`, and `zig_ident.IdentError` is exactly `error{BadIdent}`, so the published rule's error set is a subset of each caller's and `try` composes with no widening. The mechanism is the landed stub idiom from `glow/lower_face.rye`: same `out` type, same `LowerError` name, a new `field` slice so a refusal record names which face refused, delegating to `zig_ident.safe_ident` with `rm.max_name_len` as the ceiling parameter. Each call site takes the hyphenated name of what it lowers. The scan's ceiling falls 15 to 13 and its comment records the reading, leaving three `max_arm_len` siblings at 31 sites each and nine singletons. Touches no module source outside `glow/`, no ceiling any peer watches beyond this arc's own, no ledger row, no roster row, and no peer-claimed path -- the check read overlap_peer=0 over all three.
